"""Open tiers of the pagoda and the mainmast, measured: where a prism of the blueprint stands for legs, a tube, fins
and bulwarks with open space between them (under half of its footprint solid in the reference's own sections),
the model draws what `ship:slice pjsb010 --section y=...` shows there instead of the solid prism: runs of similar
cuts every 0.1 m, each drawn from its middle cut and clipped to the prism's footprint, and 8 cm plates for the
decks and ceilings vertical probes (`--probe x,z`) cross within its height. The mainmast's tripod legs are
nagato_masts struts and are left out here. Runtime frame.

TIERS[structure id] = [(y0, y1, [piece, ...]), ...]; a piece is ('c', x, z, radius), a round column, or
('p', ((x, z), ...)), an outline (thin outlines are 6 cm bulwarks, windscreens and fins).
"""

